<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rachamalla IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 975–986</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rachamalla IV was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ganga-dynasty">Western Ganga dynasty</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> in the late 10th century. His minister and general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chavundaraya">Chavundaraya</a> commissioned the colossal statue of Bahubali (Gommateshwara) at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shravanabelagola">Shravanabelagola</a> around 983, one of the greatest monuments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jainism</a>, and wrote an important early work of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> prose.</p></div>
